WEBVTT

00:00:05.969 --> 00:00:08.330
The world moves so fast today.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.300
People forget how much better they had it as kids.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.239
When hours seemed like days.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.820
And a favorite toy could be a child's best friend.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.940
Toys are powerful things, you know.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.439
They are vessels for the imagination imbued with life.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.799
Through the simple act of play.

00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:53.179
Mercer's taking too many risks.

00:00:53.679 --> 00:00:56.140
Lex took a gamble on her, and it's paying off.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.859
Look at the success she's had with the Daily Planet.

00:00:58.859 --> 00:01:04.500
Lex didn't know she was funneling all of Luther Corp's holdings into one highly experimental bioweapon.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.500
And now she's lost the prototype.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.620
I move for a vote of no confidence.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:10.819
Yeah, I second the motion.

00:01:10.819 --> 00:01:12.659
All those in favor of making a change?

00:01:13.459 --> 00:01:14.900
Aye.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.819
That is, I agree it's time for a change, but not quite how you mean it.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.420
Oliver Queen, what are you doing in enemy camp?

00:01:23.219 --> 00:01:24.980
I'm actually the one who called this meeting.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:26.579
Tess sends her...

00:01:26.739 --> 00:01:31.739
regrets, but she's on her way to Dubai overseeing some of our international interests.

00:01:31.739 --> 00:01:32.739
What do you mean our?

00:01:32.739 --> 00:01:39.980
With Tessa's cooperation, I purchased controlling interests in Luther Corp.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:46.439
That barracuda went behind our backs and helped you with a hostile takeover.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.439
Mm-mm.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:52.439
You know, I really don't think that the Luther Court board should be lecturing me on ethics, ma'am.

00:01:52.439 --> 00:01:56.439
After all, you've been using the world as your own personal playground for way too long.

00:01:56.439 --> 00:02:00.439
The world is much better off because of the Luther's, and no pampered playboy is going to destroy their legacy.

00:02:00.439 --> 00:03:16.039
destroy their legacy.

00:03:16.039 --> 00:03:18.039
Tell me that the bed was already wobbling.

00:03:18.039 --> 00:03:27.819
It's made of solid oak.

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:29.819
What do you say we find out how strong the floor is?

00:03:29.819 --> 00:03:32.819
Where do you get all the energy?

00:03:32.819 --> 00:03:35.819
How would you like to see another sunset?

00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:38.819
We could start our night all over again.

00:03:38.819 --> 00:03:41.819
Head west, find a sandy beach.

00:03:41.819 --> 00:03:46.659
I love you being so romantic, Clark.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:50.659
But there's something that I would love even more than a trip to the truck.

00:03:50.659 --> 00:03:54.460
Just ask, and it's your eyes.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:04:02.409
I want to help you when you're out of the show.

00:04:02.409 --> 00:04:03.409
Missopolis.

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:08.729
Well, I'm not so sure that...

00:04:08.729 --> 00:04:09.729
Park.

00:04:09.729 --> 00:04:12.729
When I stopped that bullet and saved Doctor Girl's life,

00:04:12.729 --> 00:04:15.729
it was the most amazing feeling I've ever had.

00:04:15.729 --> 00:04:18.730
I got to use my new powers the way I always planned to.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.730
Lana, even with your strength and speed,

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:23.730
it's still dangerous out there.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.730
You've protected me for years.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.730
But this is who I am now.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:33.740
It's the life I want.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:47.040
And I want to share it with you.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.040
All I've ever wanted was someone to share my life with.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:53.589
To work.

00:04:53.589 --> 00:04:57.000
with me side by side.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.529
Just like my mom and dad did.

00:05:01.529 --> 00:05:02.529
With my abilities, I never thought to...

00:05:02.529 --> 00:05:04.529
Clark, stop.

00:05:04.529 --> 00:05:05.529
I'm right here.

00:05:05.529 --> 00:05:27.310
Hey, there was some sort of an explosion at Luther Corp.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.310
The news was saying it was a bomb.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.310
Oh my God.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.310
Does anyone hurt?

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:33.310
Apparently everyone in the board of directors was killed.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:36.310
Oliver was there. He's in the hospital.

00:05:36.310 --> 00:06:16.500
Well, if it is a Metropolis's newest power couple.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.500
How you doing, Oliver?

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.500
I'm all right.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.500
Nothing a dry martini can't cure.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:24.699
Are there any other survivors?

00:06:24.699 --> 00:06:25.699
Survivors?

00:06:25.699 --> 00:06:27.699
You're the only one.

00:06:27.699 --> 00:06:30.699
They said the table protected you from the blast.

00:06:30.699 --> 00:06:32.699
Oliver, do you have any idea who did this?

00:06:32.699 --> 00:06:36.110
Angry shareholder, maybe.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:39.110
I just bought a controlling stake in Luther Corp.

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:42.110
I was meeting with the board to announce it.

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:48.110
If you're trying to erase the Luther from Luther Corp, then there's one obvious choice for who was behind this attack.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:49.110
Lex.

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:55.800
You know, if he was going to come after anyone, Lana, I would assume it would be you.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.800
You were the one that really got under his skin.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.050
Or should I say,

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:01.050
into it.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.050
That biotech that you commandeered, that was his lifeline.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:06.050
It was his last chance of recovery.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:09.050
I think probably meant more to him than his entire company.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:13.329
Do you remember anything before the blast?

00:07:13.329 --> 00:07:19.459
Something that could help us figure out if Lex is behind this?

00:07:19.459 --> 00:07:20.459
No.

00:07:20.459 --> 00:07:22.459
No, I didn't see anything.

00:07:22.459 --> 00:07:28.810
Don't worry, Oliver.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:30.810
I promise we're going to find out who did this.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:59.430
Oliver's lucky to be alive.

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:06.360
Looks like the bomb went off over here.

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:11.699
There's pieces in the walls everywhere.

00:08:11.699 --> 00:08:15.699
Clark, are you okay?

00:08:15.699 --> 00:08:18.699
It was kryptonite.

00:08:18.699 --> 00:08:33.149
Looks like this silver shard was part of the bone, but...

00:08:33.149 --> 00:08:36.149
Why would they use Meteor Rock?

00:08:36.149 --> 00:08:39.149
It's not the first time it's been used to make a bomb more powerful.

00:08:39.149 --> 00:08:44.259
Whoa, what was that?

00:08:44.259 --> 00:08:48.860
Whatever it was, Lana, I don't feel a kryptonite anymore.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:56.889
Maybe it was treated with something that lost its charge when I moved the chip.

00:08:56.889 --> 00:08:57.889
Queen Industries.

00:08:57.889 --> 00:09:00.889
Clark, I think that Oliver knows more than he's saying.

00:09:00.889 --> 00:09:01.889
than he's saying.

00:09:01.889 --> 00:09:02.889
Lana, it's a big company.

00:09:02.889 --> 00:09:04.889
They make thousands of chips a year.

00:09:04.889 --> 00:09:06.889
Why would you think Oliver would be responsible?

00:09:06.889 --> 00:09:09.889
I don't, but doesn't it seem like he's covering something?

00:09:09.889 --> 00:09:12.889
But why would he hide anything from me?

00:09:12.889 --> 00:09:15.889
He's done it before, Clark.

00:09:15.889 --> 00:09:19.889
When I tracked Lex to Cuba, Oliver showed up.

00:09:19.889 --> 00:09:23.360
He was there to kill Lex.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:29.139
Why didn't you tell me about this?

00:09:29.139 --> 00:09:33.139
I thought that I talked him down, but obviously he still has his own agenda.

00:09:33.139 --> 00:09:37.440
I think that you should show him the chip and get him.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.440
Show him the chip and give him a chance to explain.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:41.440
No, we can't trust him anymore.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:44.440
If he's so obsessed with killing life that he went behind my back,

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:46.440
I don't want to pull him in any deeper.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:58.429
Whatever Oliver is hiding, we'll figure it out on our own.

00:09:58.429 --> 00:10:00.429
The game has begun.

00:10:00.429 --> 00:10:09.710
Although even the finest plan can't guarantee a flawless execution.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:20.980
Apparently, Miss Mercer wasn't in the room,

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:26.500
and Oliver Queen survived.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:35.940
I'll be sure to tie up any loose that as Mr. Luther.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.820
Meanwhile,

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:42.820
We've already begun round two.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:50.210
Time for our next move.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:11:24.830
Your heart rate's a little higher than normal, Mr. Queen.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:28.389
Really?

00:11:28.389 --> 00:11:31.389
I'm sure the view has that effect on all your patients.

00:11:31.389 --> 00:11:36.389
Well, with the pain meds you're on, I'm afraid,

00:11:36.389 --> 00:11:39.389
this is the only view you're getting tonight.

00:11:39.389 --> 00:11:40.389
Rest.

00:11:40.389 --> 00:11:45.820
Looks like someone's making a speedy recovery.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:47.820
Yeah, not quick enough, trust me.

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:48.820
Well, I'm good.

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:51.820
I'm guessing you didn't get me over here to spoon you chicken soup.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:52.820
No.

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:55.820
Listen, I need you to pull an address off a Queen Industry's database.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:57.820
It's an engineer that I fired six years ago.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.820
His name's Winslow Shot.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:02.820
And you think this ex-employee is behind the bomb?

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.820
I hired him right out at MIT.

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:08.820
He developed explosives, anything from blowing out tunnels to breaking up kidney stones.

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:12.820
It's pretty high price for someone you handed a pink slip to.

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:14.820
What happened?

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:16.820
Yeah, high-pressed job.

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:17.820
He snapped.

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:22.820
He started bringing toys to work, whatever, right?

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:27.820
But then he started hiding explosives inside the toys.

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:33.820
And that's when I realized Winslow was thinking a little bit too far outside the toy box.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:36.820
Hmm.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:41.820
Why are you telling me this when you have your very own personal bomb squad in Clark and Lana?

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:45.820
Look, give me ten minutes with one of your satellites, and I'll get them to go and get him.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:46.820
No, Chloe, we can't tell Clark.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:54.570
Clark. Winslow could have attacked me any time he won in the past six years.

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:57.570
He chose the night I took over Luther Corp to do it.

00:12:57.570 --> 00:13:03.009
A toy boy may have pulled the pin, but I think he's working for Lex.

00:13:03.009 --> 00:13:07.480
So you're not actually interested in tracking this Winslow guy down.

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:09.480
You just want him to lead you to Lex.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:15.059
And you want Clark to stay out of your way.

00:13:15.059 --> 00:13:20.860
Chloe, you know Clark would never agree to do what needs to be done to get rid of Lex forever.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:26.950
You're talking about killing him, man.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:30.950
I'm talking about ending this reign of terror that's been consuming us all lately.

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:35.919
You want to tell him the truth here?

00:13:35.919 --> 00:13:37.919
You want to tell him the truth or you want to protect him?

00:13:37.919 --> 00:13:41.740
Lex tried to kill me.

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:43.740
You know he's coming after Clark next.

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:45.740
Chloe, he knows his secret.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:49.740
Did you honestly live with yourself if you let something happen to Clark?

00:13:49.740 --> 00:14:10.620
Holly, what are you doing here?

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:14.799
You know Oliver.

00:14:14.799 --> 00:14:17.799
Even the blast of a bomb won't rattle his work ethic.

00:14:17.799 --> 00:14:21.799
He asked me to come in and pull some of the files from the Luther Court deal.

00:14:21.799 --> 00:14:23.799
That's funny.

00:14:23.799 --> 00:14:27.799
Because I would think the Queen Industries could free up at least one employee to run his errands for him.

00:14:27.799 --> 00:14:28.799
for him.

00:14:28.799 --> 00:14:31.799
Yeah, well, I'm not exactly a brink security truck,

00:14:31.799 --> 00:14:33.799
but Oliver knows he can trust me.

00:14:33.799 --> 00:14:38.940
I thought I could too.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.940
You're chasing down a lead on the bombing for him, aren't you?

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:48.440
Chloe, you don't understand?

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:51.440
Lana told me about Oliver's vendetta against Lex.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.440
He knows that I would try to stop him.

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:55.440
That's why he would lie, but I don't know why you would.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:57.440
Because I don't want to lose you, Clark.

00:14:57.440 --> 00:15:01.440
Lex knows that the meteor rocks are poisonous to Kryptonians.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:03.440
He knows your weakness.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:05.440
He could kill you.

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:06.440
That doesn't mean I'm supposed to.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:08.440
to kill him first, Chloe.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:11.440
No matter what Oliver said to you, Lex and I are not in a battle to the death.

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:13.440
Open your eyes, Clark.

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:15.440
Lex declared war on you years ago.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:17.440
He's known your secret for months.

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:19.440
Why have you not done anything yet?

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:21.440
I'm focused on the future.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.440
On using my abilities to help people.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.360
I don't want to live in the past.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.360
But that's exactly what you're doing.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:33.360
You think that Lex is still that same man you saved on the bridge eight years ago?

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:36.360
You're not recognizing the monster he's become.

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:37.360
So because I'm not going to kill some war.

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:39.360
I'm not going to kill someone. I'm in denial.

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:43.059
When you were taken over by Brainiac,

00:15:43.059 --> 00:15:46.909
you could have destroyed the world, Chloe.

00:15:46.909 --> 00:16:02.159
But I refuse to kill you.

00:16:02.159 --> 00:16:04.159
It's Oliver's top suspect Winslow's shot.

00:16:04.159 --> 00:16:08.659
He used to work at Star Labs.

00:16:08.659 --> 00:16:10.659
Oliver thinks he would lead us to Lex.

00:16:10.659 --> 00:16:40.620
Don't worry. Be careful.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.620
Can I help you?

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.620
I certainly hope so.

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:47.620
Could you direct me to Oliver Queen's room? I have a delivery for him.

00:16:47.620 --> 00:17:05.809
Lana.

00:17:05.809 --> 00:17:12.700
You found a necklace.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:15.700
After all the pain it caused you, I'm surprised you still have it.

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:19.700
How could I throw away something that means so much?

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:26.640
I still remember seeing you wear this in high school.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:31.369
I couldn't get within five feet of you, without falling over.

00:17:31.369 --> 00:17:34.369
And even after your ship got rid of the kryptonite,

00:17:34.369 --> 00:17:37.369
there always seemed to be something standing in our way.

00:17:37.369 --> 00:17:40.160
Not anymore.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.660
We're together now, Lana.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.660
I'm not going to let anyone take that away from us.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:52.660
Clark, I talked to Dr. Girl about what happened with the kryptonite.

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:53.660
It wasn't the chip tonight.

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:54.660
It wasn't the chip.

00:17:54.660 --> 00:18:03.000
It was me.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.000
So besides strength and speed, you can destroy kryptonite.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:08.000
No. Dr. Grohl says I absorbed it.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:10.000
But I'm worried, Clark.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:13.000
If Lex built this as a weapon,

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.000
what if you were the target?

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:18.470
But Lex isn't wearing it, Lana, you are.

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:21.470
Look, we're gonna figure this out.

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:24.470
But we need to stay focused on tracking down this bomber

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:26.470
before he causes any more damage.

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:30.039
Did you find anything?

00:18:30.039 --> 00:18:31.039
Yeah.

00:18:31.039 --> 00:18:35.819
You were right.

00:18:35.819 --> 00:18:36.819
Oliver was hiding something.

00:18:36.819 --> 00:18:38.819
He thinks the bomber was someone he used to work for.

00:18:38.819 --> 00:18:42.839
I went to that address listed there,

00:18:42.839 --> 00:18:44.839
but he doesn't live there anymore.

00:18:44.839 --> 00:18:48.839
According to this, Mr. Schott is a pretty prolific inventor.

00:18:48.839 --> 00:18:51.839
He felt a lot of patents for Star Labs.

00:18:51.839 --> 00:18:56.470
A guy like this, he wouldn't just stop registering his research

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:58.470
because Oliver let him go.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.470
So maybe the Patent Office has a current address for him.

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:05.940
If this guy's working for Lex, we're dealing with a lot more than just some toy maker.

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:09.940
If Lex put things in motion, he has planned three moves ahead.

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:10.940
And now that he is not that he is not.

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:14.940
And now that he is nothing to lose, he's more dangerous than ever.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:33.000
The hell?

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:37.440
How does it feel to not be in control for once?

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:38.440
Untie me right now.

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:42.710
That wouldn't be very much fun?

00:19:42.710 --> 00:19:52.039
Well, I get it. I get it.

00:19:52.039 --> 00:19:53.039
The, uh...

00:19:53.039 --> 00:19:57.900
The children's wards two floors up, you know.

00:19:57.900 --> 00:19:58.900
Excuse me?

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:01.900
The balloons, monkey, the ridiculous costume you're wearing.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.900
You're a clown, right? Aren't you a clown?

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:11.589
I am Winslow's shot.

00:20:11.589 --> 00:20:15.589
You called me one of Starlab's greatest minds, and then you fired me.

00:20:15.589 --> 00:20:21.900
Yeah, I remember you know.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:25.900
Well, it's good to see you're still playing with toys.

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:27.900
Come on, man.

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:29.900
How much for the ape?

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:38.269
I don't need your money anymore, Mr. Queen.

00:20:38.269 --> 00:20:41.519
I found someone new to work with.

00:20:41.519 --> 00:20:45.519
Someone who appreciates my genius.

00:20:45.519 --> 00:20:50.599
None other than Lex Luthor himself?

00:20:50.599 --> 00:20:53.599
Well, that's impressive.

00:20:53.599 --> 00:20:58.009
I thought he was dead.

00:20:58.009 --> 00:21:00.009
You are the one who was supposed to be dead.

00:21:00.009 --> 00:21:03.009
You should have died in that example.

00:21:03.009 --> 00:21:04.009
Like everyone else!

00:21:04.009 --> 00:21:06.009
You seem like you're getting angry, Winslow.

00:21:06.009 --> 00:21:08.009
Maybe you should take your toys and go home.

00:21:08.009 --> 00:21:17.920
Actually, I made a toy just for you.

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:27.710
After this little fella clangs his symbols together 53 times.

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:34.759
Fifty-three, huh?

00:21:34.759 --> 00:21:39.099
Seems a little arbitrary, doesn't it?

00:21:39.099 --> 00:21:42.099
I filed 53 patents working for you.

00:21:42.099 --> 00:21:46.099
Queen Industries made millions and I got nothing.

00:21:46.099 --> 00:22:03.269
I appreciated my artistry just a whole day.

00:22:03.269 --> 00:22:05.269
Unlocked the other cup.

00:22:05.269 --> 00:22:07.269
Come on, 28 and counting.

00:22:07.269 --> 00:22:09.269
Zobo's not gonna slow down anytime soon.

00:22:09.269 --> 00:22:20.279
I swear I'll break every one of your artistic little fingers.

00:22:20.279 --> 00:22:23.279
Now tell me, where can I find Lex?

00:22:23.279 --> 00:22:39.190
This is the last known address that Patten Office had for him.

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:43.190
Chloe mentioned is Winslow and I had a thing for toys.

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:55.400
And I'm guessing he still lives here.

00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:56.400
Clark.

00:22:56.400 --> 00:22:59.970
There's a wireless camera inside this doll.

00:22:59.970 --> 00:23:05.329
Someone's watching us.

00:23:05.329 --> 00:23:07.329
I can guess who it is.

00:23:07.329 --> 00:23:09.329
Lex likes to keep an eye on the people that work for him.

00:23:09.329 --> 00:23:19.380
for it.

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:24.680
Lana, look at this.

00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:25.680
It's Metropolis.

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:29.680
Winsle must have played out the bombing here before the attack.

00:23:29.680 --> 00:23:32.680
If that's the case, then Daily Planet is Lex's next target.

00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:43.549
Excuse me, Mr. Queen.

00:23:43.549 --> 00:23:45.549
It's the time for your medicine.

00:23:45.549 --> 00:23:55.579
Queen.

00:23:55.579 --> 00:23:57.579
I just delivered a balloonogram and the guy attacked me.

00:23:57.579 --> 00:24:00.579
Here, let me help you.

00:24:00.579 --> 00:24:01.579
Thank you.

00:24:01.579 --> 00:24:03.579
Thank you so much.

00:24:03.579 --> 00:24:04.579
You?

00:24:04.579 --> 00:24:06.579
You're Winslow shot.

00:24:06.579 --> 00:24:07.579
No, don't untie him!

00:24:07.579 --> 00:24:08.579
Tie him!

00:24:08.579 --> 00:24:25.930
I win.

00:24:25.930 --> 00:24:38.680
I just picked up Chloe from the hospital.

00:24:38.680 --> 00:24:40.680
She's okay.

00:24:40.680 --> 00:24:42.680
But this toy man guy got away.

00:24:42.680 --> 00:24:44.680
Keep looking, Lana.

00:24:44.680 --> 00:24:51.039
Call me crazy, Clark, but isn't there a bomb you should be finding?

00:24:51.039 --> 00:24:54.039
Tracing that camera's signal made by the only chance to find Lex.

00:24:54.039 --> 00:24:56.039
And Lana's already searching for the bomb at the Daily Planet.

00:24:56.039 --> 00:24:57.039
Have you had any luck?

00:24:57.039 --> 00:25:02.039
The feeds of the camera's been cut, but it was definitely broadcasting to a single receiver.

00:25:02.039 --> 00:25:04.039
You found Lex?

00:25:04.039 --> 00:25:08.019
Well, I managed to sneak past the latest gaggle of ghost routers and ping the original

00:25:08.039 --> 00:25:10.039
IP address that Winslow was sending to.

00:25:10.039 --> 00:25:11.039
Where is he?

00:25:11.039 --> 00:25:13.039
Where sort of depends on when.

00:25:13.039 --> 00:25:16.039
Clark, Lex has been on the move this whole time.

00:25:16.039 --> 00:25:18.039
I thought Lex was immobilized.

00:25:18.039 --> 00:25:20.039
Lex may have been immobilized,

00:25:20.039 --> 00:25:24.039
but his IP address is still leaping tall wireless towers

00:25:24.039 --> 00:25:25.039
in a single bound.

00:25:25.039 --> 00:25:28.039
Now, I programmed the signal into one of Oliver's satellites

00:25:28.039 --> 00:25:30.039
and synced it with my PDA.

00:25:30.039 --> 00:25:33.039
I made you a Lex tracker.

00:25:33.039 --> 00:25:37.039
Now Oliver's satellite is about to pass out of range.

00:25:37.039 --> 00:25:38.039
You only have 10 minutes.

00:25:38.039 --> 00:25:49.200
before the signal is gone and Lex disappears again.

00:25:49.200 --> 00:25:52.200
Clerk, I searched every room and I can't find the bomb anywhere.

00:25:52.200 --> 00:25:53.200
Like you said, we're a team.

00:25:53.200 --> 00:26:38.049
It's on the roof.

00:26:38.049 --> 00:26:40.049
Clark with that much crypticin, I could take out half the city.

00:26:40.049 --> 00:26:45.509
Lock, Kent, and Lana Leigh.

00:26:45.509 --> 00:26:47.509
Welcome to your destiny.

00:26:47.509 --> 00:26:50.509
You've destroyed me in every way.

00:26:50.509 --> 00:26:56.950
So now, I'm going to take away what matters most to you.

00:26:56.950 --> 00:26:58.950
Lex.

00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:02.930
Do you know what people remember about the greatest Star Cross romance

00:27:02.950 --> 00:27:10.970
not how the lovers met, but the way the relationship tragically ended.

00:27:10.970 --> 00:27:14.970
The skin alone is wearing designed to absorb enough meteor rock

00:27:14.970 --> 00:27:20.279
that you'll never be able to go near her again.

00:27:20.279 --> 00:27:23.279
You're a coward, Lex. Come out here, face us.

00:27:23.279 --> 00:27:25.279
No, Mark.

00:27:25.279 --> 00:27:28.279
It's time for you to face your defining moment.

00:27:28.279 --> 00:27:33.279
You can walk away, sacrificing innocent lives to stay together,

00:27:33.279 --> 00:27:35.279
or defuse the bomb.

00:27:35.279 --> 00:27:50.509
I'll sacrifice your love forever.

00:27:50.509 --> 00:30:05.589
You have to.

00:30:05.589 --> 00:30:07.589
How much it hurts right now, Clark.

00:30:07.589 --> 00:30:10.589
But if you go after Lex like this, you will kill him.

00:30:10.589 --> 00:30:16.890
What he's done to us, Lana, he needs to be stopped.

00:30:16.890 --> 00:30:20.890
I promise you, I will help you to punish Lex.

00:30:20.890 --> 00:30:30.059
But if you kill him, you will lose so much more than just us being together.

00:30:30.059 --> 00:31:37.430
You'll lose yourself.

00:31:37.430 --> 00:31:42.630
Lex deserved to die, Chloe.

00:31:42.630 --> 00:31:44.630
You certainly made sure he got what he deserved.

00:31:44.630 --> 00:31:47.630
They identified the remains as Lexus.

00:31:47.630 --> 00:31:53.890
And what does Clark think?

00:31:53.890 --> 00:31:55.890
That Winslow turned on, Lex.

00:31:55.890 --> 00:31:59.890
Pieces of a toy bomb were found in the wreckage.

00:31:59.890 --> 00:32:11.259
Yeah, well, that makes sense.

00:32:11.259 --> 00:32:13.259
Wouldn't be like Winslow to play a game he can't win?

00:32:13.259 --> 00:32:20.789
Are you seriously gonna let another man take the blame for something you did?

00:32:20.789 --> 00:32:26.359
Chloe, Winslow, Winslow, Winslow, is already a killer.

00:32:26.359 --> 00:32:28.359
He blew up all those people at Luther Corp.

00:32:28.359 --> 00:32:31.359
He was about ready to take down the entire daily planet.

00:32:31.359 --> 00:32:33.700
One more destiny.

00:32:33.700 --> 00:32:34.700
not gonna make a difference.

00:32:34.700 --> 00:32:37.700
Are you listening to yourself?

00:32:37.700 --> 00:32:39.700
Oliver, you've really crossed a line here.

00:32:39.700 --> 00:32:41.700
Lex is dead.

00:32:41.700 --> 00:32:43.700
The world is safer because of it.

00:32:43.700 --> 00:32:44.700
Clark is safe again.

00:32:44.700 --> 00:32:45.700
This is murder.

00:32:45.700 --> 00:32:49.140
This is justice.

00:32:49.140 --> 00:32:51.140
Although Clark may not be able to accept that.

00:32:51.140 --> 00:32:57.460
You know what I did was right.

00:32:57.460 --> 00:33:00.460
Please don't stand there and look so innocent.

00:33:00.460 --> 00:33:04.460
You know, I did a little video viewing of my own.

00:33:04.460 --> 00:33:08.460
Seems a certain meteor freak named Sebastian Kane

00:33:08.460 --> 00:33:09.460
died in.

00:33:09.460 --> 00:33:13.460
at the hospital, right after he was visited by somebody who looked an awful lot like you.

00:33:13.460 --> 00:33:19.380
That was brainiac. Not me.

00:33:19.380 --> 00:33:27.109
Was it like a pretty natural instinct to protect Clark?

00:33:27.109 --> 00:33:36.299
Now that Lex's gone, you can't tell me you're not relieved.

00:33:36.299 --> 00:33:47.339
Every fiber of my conscience wants to say that's not true.

00:33:47.339 --> 00:33:49.740
But...

00:33:52.940 --> 00:33:53.940
Clark, what I did.

00:33:53.940 --> 00:34:03.279
Lex just ripped the man's heart out, Chloe.

00:34:03.279 --> 00:34:05.279
He's gonna need his friends around him right now more than ever.

00:34:05.279 --> 00:34:38.909
To cast my shadow by the holy sun.

00:34:39.909 --> 00:37:27.699
Lux already took care of that.

00:37:27.699 --> 00:37:28.699
Did you talk to Dr. Grohl?

00:37:28.699 --> 00:37:37.420
Can he help us?

00:37:37.420 --> 00:37:47.320
No.

00:37:47.320 --> 00:37:49.320
I'm gonna do everything I can to fix this, Lana.

00:37:49.320 --> 00:37:52.320
I will find a way for us to be together.

00:37:52.320 --> 00:37:54.320
Clark, he tried everything.

00:37:54.320 --> 00:38:07.909
He can't reverse the process.

00:38:07.909 --> 00:38:14.929
I love you.

00:38:14.929 --> 00:38:16.929
I know what I need to do with my life now.

00:38:16.929 --> 00:38:24.070
So precious.

00:38:24.070 --> 00:38:30.750
And to be able to protect that, that's an amazing gift.

00:38:30.750 --> 00:38:34.829
I know you feel the same way.

00:38:38.900 --> 00:38:39.900
What we have is beautiful.

00:38:39.900 --> 00:38:47.760
We made our choice on that roof.

00:38:47.760 --> 00:38:48.760
And I'm just.

00:38:48.760 --> 00:38:51.219
I know we would do it again.

00:38:51.219 --> 00:38:53.119
Because both of us are driven to do this,

00:38:53.119 --> 00:38:58.980
even if we can't do it together.

00:38:58.980 --> 00:39:04.820
Don't leave again, Lula.

00:39:04.820 --> 00:39:09.739
Even if we can't be together, I want you in my life.

00:39:09.739 --> 00:39:11.400
That's where you're stronger than me.

00:39:11.400 --> 00:39:21.349
See you on the street every day.

00:39:21.349 --> 00:39:26.699
I'll not be able to stay.

00:39:26.699 --> 00:40:45.800
Clark, don't.

00:40:45.800 --> 00:40:48.579
That night at the cemetery when I introduced you

00:40:48.579 --> 00:40:53.980
to my mom and dad, you told me that I would never be alone.

00:40:53.980 --> 00:40:57.719
That my mom would always be watching over me

00:40:57.719 --> 00:40:58.420
for any child.

00:40:58.440 --> 00:41:02.829
I will always be with you.

